      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's important to be very careful when dealing with blood pressure medication. Administering a double dose immediately to counter an missed dose can potentially put him at risk, as the effects of the medication may already be in effect and not yet worn off. It's best to contact his doctor or his regular pharmacy to get specific, personalized advice. They may want to come in for a prescription refill or even a quick check-up depending on the circumstances. Informing them of your husband's experience can help them provide proper guidance. If you believe he's in immediate distress or if his symptoms persist, it's better to err on the side of seeking emergency medical attention. Your health and safety is the most important priority.",
